{
  "schema": "woof-landuse-to-fuel-v1",
  "notes": [
    "Fuel categories are Anderson (1982) 1-13, plus 14 for no fuel, the NFUEL_CAT convention of WRF-SFIRE's namelist.fire.",
    "Read by woof.static.fuel. A row is data, not code: changing a mapping is an edit here, and the static build fingerprints this file's bytes into the fuel receipt.",
    "The land-use rows are woof's own data choice, not a WRF or WPS table. Every land-use class is assigned the Anderson model whose dominant carrier (grass, shrub, timber litter, timber understory) matches the class description. Water, lakes, urban, built-up and LCZ classes, snow and ice, and barren classes map to 14.",
    "Cropland is irrigated or harvested in most of the year. The table follows LANDFIRE, which classes agriculture as NB3 (non-burnable), only for USGS 3 (irrigated cropland). Dryland cropland and pasture, and the cropland mosaics, map to 1 (short grass), the cured stubble and pasture that carry fire after harvest.",
    "The FBFM40 rows group Scott and Burgan (2005, RMRS-GTR-153) models by fuel type and load. GR1-GR2 (short, low-load grass) map to 1. GR3-GR9 (grass 1.5 ft or deeper) map to 3. GS1-GS4 (grass-shrub) map to 2. SH5, SH7 and SH9 (tall, high-load shrub) map to 4. SH1 and SH6 map to 5. SH2 maps to 6. SH3, SH4 and SH8 (humid shrub) map to 7. TU1 and TU3 (grass-dominated understory) map to 2. TU2, TU4 and TU5 map to 10. TL1, TL3 and TL4 (compact conifer litter) map to 8. TL2, TL6, TL8 and TL9 (broadleaf and long-needle litter) map to 9. TL5 and TL7 (litter with downed wood) map to 10. SB1-SB4 map to 11, 12, 13 and 13. NB91-NB99 map to 14. This crosswalk is woof's own grouping, not a LANDFIRE product."
  ],
